<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Code shared by the MAUI app and GetThereAPI: the contracts and enums they exchange, and the
    ticket extraction both run.

    Extraction (Extraction/) used to live in its own GetThereExtraction project. It was folded in
    here because its consumer set was identical to this project's — nothing referenced one without
    the other — so the separate assembly bought nothing but another node in the graph. The reason
    it is shared at all is unchanged and still worth stating: it used to be server-only in
    GetThereAPI, which meant every import path needed a network call and an account, so a
    signed-out user could not import a ticket and neither could a signed-in one with no signal.
    Both sides now run the same code, so they cannot disagree.

    What deliberately stayed behind in GetThereAPI:
      - PdfTicketExtractor  — PdfPig is the heaviest dependency here and the AOT/trimming risk on
                              iOS is real. PDF import therefore still needs an account.
      - ICalTicketExtractor — Ical.Net, same reasoning, lower value.
      - PkPassTicketExtractor — BCL-only and otherwise portable, but it throws GetThereAPI's
                              AppException, and untangling that is a separate change.

    Note this project is referenced by the MAUI app, so anything landing here has to be safe for a
    mobile build. That is why SharedAuth is separate: ASP.NET Identity, EF Core and OpenTelemetry
    would drag the whole server stack into the app.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Extraction only. Decodes the barcode formats transport tickets use; both consumers of this
         project already reference both packages directly, so this pins nothing new. -->
    <PackageReference Include="ZXing.Net" />
    <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Dummy Run target -->
  <Target Name="Run" />

</Project>
